\ChangesListline {added}{Added\nobreakspace {}(dev)}{Describe an ITS architecture based on the 3 typical components described in the Background section, namely: domain model, user mode, tutor model. The base user model is given by the state of acquisition of the knowledge components defined in the domain model. In addition it is augmented with the output of a gBKT model. The gBKT model on its side is fed with a tuple (L0, T) that is the output of a gTransformer model. The output of the user model goes into the tutor model that makes the instruction decisions.}{3}
\ChangesListline {added}{Added\nobreakspace {}(dev)}{Describe the methodology for the experiments. We will describe gBKT as a traditional BKT model augmented with a gTransformer model that ouputs L0 and T parameters. These parameters are the projections of a z context vector and they encapsulate the longitudinal context of the student learning trajectory. Explain that we validate gBKT comparing it with a traditional BKT model and demonstrating that it outperforms the traditional BKT model in terms of accuracy. Briefly describe the architecture of gTransformer (summarizing the architecture explained in the MDPI paper) and explain that it has been trained with the ASSISTments 2009 dataset. Explain that the same L0, T parameters are used also to augment the student model.}{3}
\ChangesListline {added}{Added\nobreakspace {}(dev)}{Describe the results of the experiments and discuss the implications of the results and applications.}{3}
